      "units": "gDW/g glucose",
      "how": "Model: DIRECT mass-balance yield per cell = ΔDW / ∫(q_glc·DW)dt — grams dry weight made per gram glucose consumed (a mass ratio, robust to the steady-state assumption; the μ/(q_glc·M_glc) shortcut agrees at balanced growth but runs ~7% higher and noisier). Graded against curated experimental measurements (band 0.355–0.444 gDW/g glucose; sources shown in the plot). The red dashed line is the theoretical-max stoichiometric ceiling (0.538 gDW/g glucose) — a model value above it is a first-principles violation.",
